**How to implement.** The button for step 422's message: the user chooses, on an unmatched group's row of the split panel, the setup the capture was taken over (AGENTS.md 'Every user action is a semantic Elmish message. The button and the test send the same message'; 001 §O 'Data dialog: … the key split with a matched / unmatched table'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S12.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, beside `dataSplitGroupRow` and `dataSplitOfferToggle` (step 324): `static member dataSplitGroupSetupChoice (key : DataRowKey) : ConstructorUiId`, `DataSplitGroupSetup_<the key's file stem>`, documented in one line. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs`, the split panel (step 324): the row of a group whose matching is `GroupWithoutMatch (SplitKeyNameErr _)` or `GroupWithoutMatch (SplitKeySetupErr _)` keeps its `unmatched — <describe>` text and gains, on the same row, `Record over:` and a `ComboBox` carrying `dataSplitGroupSetupChoice key`, listing `model.kitSetups`' names in kit order with nothing selected, whose choice sends `OfferSplitGroupOver (key, <the chosen name>)`; a kit holding no setup shows no box. An offered group keeps its toggle (`dataSplitOfferToggle`), so a group offered this way is ticked and untickable like any offer. No other control or text changes. (3) Tests, in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs` (step 324), mounted as its facts mount the Data step: `an unreadable group's row offers the kit's setups, and choosing one sends OfferSplitGroupOver`: over a model whose split lists `Darkness` unmatched for `SplitKeyNameErr` and a kit holding `Bench` and `Bench (2)`, the row of `Darkness` carries `DataSplitGroupSetup_Darkness` listing both names, choosing `Bench (2)` dispatches `OfferSplitGroupOver (DataRowKey "Darkness", SetupName "Bench (2)")`, and a matched or offered row carries no such box; `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also checks `dataSplitGroupSetupChoice (DataRowKey "Darkness")`'s text; `the split panel names its key column and lists each group matched, offered or unmatched, with Apply and Cancel in one row` also finds the box on the unmatched row of its fixture.

**Acceptance.** After the panel lands, an unmatched group's row MUST offer the kit's setups through `dataSplitGroupSetupChoice` and send `OfferSplitGroupOver` on a choice; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected class, including `an unreadable group's row offers the kit's setups, and choosing one sends OfferSplitGroupOver` and the widened `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` and `the split panel names its key column and lists each group matched, offered or unmatched, with Apply and Cancel in one row`, its count rising by 1; kit-acceptance MUST pass over `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s41 invariants MUST pass.
